    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW26gJem5BAwyANWeVGb6KSsV)_\n\n## Summary\nFirst piece of integrating `sp-search` / `consult-omni` with `sp-trails`: a new module `sp-trails-search` (with literate doc).\n\n- `sp-trails-search` (`o` in `sp-trails-map`, `j` in the `C-c s m` menu) asks which consult-omni search to run (web and notes, web, scholarly, my notes), starts/resumes a trail if none is current, and runs it.\n- `RET` on a result still opens it in the external browser, and also adds it to the trail as a `TOREAD` page (query, source, DOI, authors kept as properties). Nothing is recorded while only browsing results.\n- The page hangs under the trail page at point, else under the trail. The browser extension later reports the same URL, which `sp-trails-add-page` dedupes, and links followed from it become its children.\n- Embark action `t` records a result without opening it.\n- Done by advising `consult-omni--get-source-prop` for `:on-callback` only while a trail search runs, so no vendored code is patched.\n\nNot in this PR (listed in the doc): ripgrep results as trail nodes, linking saved views to trail nodes, recording note results.\n\n## Test plan\n- [ ] `C-c s m j`, pick \"scholarly sources\", search, `RET` on a result: opens in browser and appears under the trail in `trails.org`.\n- [ ] Same with point on a page of the trail: the new page is its child.\n- [ ] In the minibuffer, `C-x`-style Embark then `t`: recorded, nothing opens.\n- [ ] CI tangle-check. Not run in Emacs: the container has none, the `.el` was extracted from the doc by script and paren-balanced.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCibxqie5suY1BNy9m)_",
